Triangle $ECB$ has sides $8,15,17$, and $8^2+15^2=17^2$, so it has a right angle at $C$. Its height to $EB$, which is the height of the trapezoid, is
\[
h=\dfrac{8\cdot15}{17}=\dfrac{120}{17}.
\]
The area is $\dfrac{20+3}{2}\cdot\dfrac{120}{17}=\dfrac{1380}{17}$, a reduced fraction, so $x-y=1380-17=\boxed{1363}$.

By symmetry the foot of the altitude from $D$ is the centre $O$ of the equilateral triangle $ABC$, and the centre $I$ of the inscribed sphere lies on $DO$ with $IO=11$. Let $M$ be the midpoint of $BC$ and $r_0=OM$ the inradius of triangle $ABC$. The plane $DOM$ is perpendicular to the face $DBC$ (it contains $DM$ and is perpendicular to $BC$), so in this plane the inscribed sphere appears as a circle of radius $11$ tangent to $OM$ at $O$ and to $DM$ at a point $T$ (drawn to scale):

